meta {
  name: Review Document
  type: http
  seq: 2
}

post {
  url: {{coreBaseUrl}}:8112/
  body: json
  auth: none
}

headers {
  Authorization: Bearer {{idToken}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "docId": "REPLACE-WITH-DOC-ID-FROM-CREATE-DOCUMENT",
    "approve": true
  }
}

docs {
  functions-core: ReviewDocument (port 8112). Admin-only (§8 item 2 — the
  real DBS verification method is an open product question; this is just the
  mechanical review-decision endpoint). The "admin" custom claim isn't
  settable via any endpoint in this codebase by design — set it out of band
  first, either:

    - via the Emulator UI's Authentication tab (http://127.0.0.1:4000/auth —
      only present when you run the full `npm run emulators:start`, not the
      `--only firestore,storage` subset used for rules tests): edit the user
      and set custom claims to {"admin": true}, or
    - via the Auth emulator's REST API using its "Bearer owner" admin
      shortcut (emulator-only — never works against real Firebase):

        curl -X POST \
          "http://127.0.0.1:9099/identitytoolkit.googleapis.com/v1/projects/demo-bridgeflex/accounts:update" \
          -H "Authorization: Bearer owner" \
          -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
          -d '{"localId": "staff-sam", "customAttributes": "{\"admin\":true}"}'

  Then sign that user back in (custom claims only appear in a freshly issued
  ID token — see auth/ requests) before running this request. Without the
  claim, expect 403 NOT_ADMIN.
}
